            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="0905" n="803" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg803"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 G 861/298A: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the High Commissioner in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-21T11:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1927—11
                                a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>49. Your 36, May 19, 10 a.m. Official announcement of Mr. Grew’s appointment made
                    last evening. You may confirm it.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d759-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d759-f1" n="44" xml:id="d759-f1-content">
                <p>Ambassador Grew presented his letter of credence to the President of Turkey on
                    October 12 (file No. 123 G 861/312).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
